Sensorium Swap

Regenerate the same modeled invariant under a different sensory hierarchy. Ask what the room is as sound, reachability, pressure, movement, temperature, threat, or symbolic relation rather than only as a picture.

Echo Epistemics

```text
projection → action or observation → world contact → returned echo → delta → model update
```

Recursive Delta Observatory

Track at least:

• predicted versus observed location;
• imagined versus perceived detail;
• egocentric versus allocentric stability;
• vividness versus accuracy;
• single-sense versus multisensory reconstruction;
• resolution cost versus decision value.

Reconstruction cues

The operator can be reconstructed from four commands:

1. Replace the internal camera with a situated self-model.
2. Give every surrounding region an address, even when it lacks detail.
3. Render by modality and resolution only when queried.
4. Preserve uncertainty and test projections against returning echoes.

Compact handle:

> **I am not the camera. I am the system that can place cameras—or operate without one.**

Practice protocol: Spherical Attention

1. Establish six anchors: front, back, left, right, above, below.
2. Place remembered objects without forcing visual imagery.
3. Encode each object as a fuzzy volume plus confidence and provenance.
4. Add a nonvisual property: reachability, expected sound, texture, temperature, or affordance.
5. Move attention behind the body without pretending the eyes have turned.
6. Rotate the modeled self while attempting to keep the surrounding model stationary.
7. Reopen the eyes or physically inspect the location.
8. Record the delta and update the model.

The training target is calibrated allocentric presence, not maximum vividness.

Multiplayer play: Have Some Fun With People

These games are consensual, inspectable, reversible, and followed by a reveal or accuracy check. They exercise perspective rather than exploit it.

1. Backspace Cartographer

One player studies a room, closes their eyes, and describes the space behind them through location, reachability, sound, and confidence. Another player checks the map and scores calibration rather than descriptive flourish.

2. Sensorium Director

A director names a familiar place and bans vision for one round. Players reconstruct it using only sound, touch, proprioception, temperature, smell, movement, or symbolism. Compare which invariants survive each carrier.

3. Resolution Auction

Players receive a limited attention budget and must decide which regions or details to resolve before answering a spatial question. Reward useful information purchased cheaply, not exhaustive description.

4. Human Camera Array

Several people stand facing different directions. Each contributes one field of observation plus uncertainty. The group assembles a shared 360-degree model, then rotates positions and measures what was preserved, lost, or invented.

5. Impossible Room

Each person adds one spatial relation to an imagined room. The group must detect when the accumulated relations become geometrically inconsistent. This turns dissonance detection into play.

6. Perspective Smuggling—Revealed

Describe the same neutral scene from several occupants’ viewpoints without naming the occupant until the end. Participants infer the embodied perspective, then inspect which sensory and social assumptions gave it away.

Multiplayer safety gate

Do not use the operator to frighten, deceive, impersonate, destabilize, or covertly manipulate an unaware person. If participants cannot inspect the rules, withdraw, or distinguish imagination from evidence, close the Gate.

Failure modes and corrections

|Failure                   |Symptom                                  |Correction                                      |
|--------------------------|-----------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|
|Internal panorama trap    |Straining for continuous photorealism    |Use sparse geometry, relations, and affordances |
|Forward-camera inheritance|Imagined view keeps turning with the face|Hold the world fixed and transform self-pose    |
|Vividness inflation       |Detailed image feels automatically true  |Preserve provenance and test against reality    |
|Symbol-location drift     |Labels float without stable geometry     |Re-anchor to body axes and known surfaces       |
|False completion          |Unknown space fills with plausible detail|Represent `unknown` explicitly                  |
|Resolution addiction      |Everything receives equal detail         |Allocate resolution by expected decision value  |
|Interpersonal misuse      |Game becomes covert influence            |Require consent, reveal, reversibility, and exit|

Money Bin deposits

• Adaptive perception: Treat resolution as an allocatable resource across the full embodied field.
• Animation and direction: Build scenes as persistent world models; render only the camera’s current view while preserving off-screen causal geometry.
• Robotics: Separate the agent’s world-state estimate from its active sensor view; maintain uncertainty behind occlusion.
• Team cognition: Fuse partial observers into a shared model without erasing disagreement or provenance.
• Memory: Store relational and multisensory reconstruction cues rather than only image-like snapshots.
• Empathy: Move the attention cursor into another body’s likely sensorium while retaining uncertainty and interface humility.
• Planning: Populate possible futures as low-resolution probability fields, then zoom where decisions require detail.
• Creativity: Change viewpoint, modality, scale, or certainty independently to generate new renderings of the same invariant.

Promotion tests

The operator advances from canonical candidate to validated doctrine only if repeated trials show improvement over an appropriate null in one or more of:

• spatial recall accuracy;
• navigation or orientation;
• transfer across sensory modalities;
• calibration of confidence;
• collaborative scene reconstruction;
• animation continuity or off-screen causal consistency;
• useful perspective-taking without increased false certainty.

Preserve failed trials and counterexamples. A compelling subjective experience is a discovery lead, not sufficient validation.